{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "What is method resolution order (MRO) and how do I see it?"}, {"role": "silicat", "content": "MRO is the order Python searches base classes for attributes/methods, computed with the C3 linearization. View it with `ClassName.__mro__` or `ClassName.mro()`.\n\n```python\nclass A: pass\nclass B(A): pass\nclass C(A): pass\nclass D(B, C): pass\n\nprint([c.__name__ for c in D.__mro__])\n# ['D', 'B', 'C', 'A', 'object']\n```"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Show diamond inheritance and how super() cooperates."}, {"role": "silicat", "content": "```python\nclass A:\n    def __init__(self):\n        print(\"A\")\n        super().__init__()\n\nclass B(A):\n    def __init__(self):\n        print(\"B\")\n        super().__init__()\n\nclass C(A):\n    def __init__(self):\n        print(\"C\")\n        super().__init__()\n\nclass D(B, C):\n    def __init__(self):\n        print(\"D\")\n        super().__init__()\n\nD()  # prints D, B, C, A — each runs once thanks to the MRO\n```"}]}
